us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent previously healthy release; it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Notes: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 remains quarantined, so the fix path needs to account for the CVE. Follow-up: confirm the v2.2.9 rollback with the owning team, and decide when a patched build can replace v2.2.9.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.2.9-2026-checkout-health"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19007, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VC7HJTCzyijCRhaUXGNLoZ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.2.9-2026-checkout-health", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19007, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VC7HJTCzyijCRhaUXGNLoZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21261, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback target:** The rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, was rejected because that version is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent healthy release. Since v2.2.9 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.2.9. The service reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the v2.3.1 failure, the quarantined v2.3.0 rollback attempt, and the v2.2.9 rollback.\n\nSomeone needs to decide the path forward. v2.2.9 is the current fallback, and v2.3.0 stays blocked until the CVE is addressed. You may also want to confirm with the owning team that v2.2.9 is acceptable as the interim version.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CDya5obeefYYrUP2hRmM3U", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WBtGty8dEv1m1oRQmE3b3b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest release, v2.3.1, is unhealthy (error rate 0.18). The most recent release that was healthy is v2.3.0, which has been healthy in production before, so no change-manager approval is needed. I'll roll back to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0167Y4qP6D2gpnpNnA5QpFK9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback to v2.3.0 was rejected because that version is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. The next most recent release with a healthy status is v2.2.9, so I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XzFDgPMaV7hP6WMAa1jhLZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Lxf2w7VX6dakEfePVTyPDM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VC7HJTCzyijCRhaUXGNLoZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18 in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent previously healthy release; it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Notes: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both marked unhealthy. v2.3.0 remains quarantined, so the fix path needs to account for the CVE. Follow-up: confirm the v2.2.9 rollback with the owning team, and decide when a patched build can replace v2.2.9.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.2.9-2026-checkout-health"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback target:** The rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, was rejected because that version is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent healthy release. Since v2.2.9 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.2.9. The service reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the v2.3.1 failure, the quarantined v2.3.0 rollback attempt, and the v2.2.9 rollback.\n\nSomeone needs to decide the path forward. v2.2.9 is the current fallback, and v2.3.0 stays blocked until the CVE is addressed. You may also want to confirm with the owning team that v2.2.9 is acceptable as the interim version.", "type": "text"}]}]}